/* book Worked example 2: Q: A TLC plate is run until the solvent front is 8.0 cm above the starting line. Spot A has moved 2.0 cm and spot B 5.6 cm. Find both Rf values and say which compound is held more strongly by the stationary phase.
   1. Rf = distance moved by the spot ÷ distance moved by the solvent front.
   2. Spot A: Rf = 2.0 / 8.0 = 0.25.
   3. Spot B: Rf = 5.6 / 8.0 = 0.70.
   4. A moved less, so it spent more time held by the stationary phase.
   Answer: Rf(A) = 0.25 and Rf(B) = 0.70; compound A is held more strongly by the stationary phase. */
